.(PUSOY DOS, PICKERING RULES - DRAFT. Uses proposed syntax, so it doesn't
  parse yet. Proposals used: 11 flag, 12 not, 14 /, 19 extends and base,
  20 jokers and wildcards. See PROPOSALS.md.

  HOW TO PLAY

  Play Pusoy Dos (see pusoy_dos.card), with these changes.

  Suit order
    Clubs (lowest), hearts, diamonds, spades (highest). So 2s is the best
    card and 3c the worst. As in the standard game, the suit decides
    between cards of the same rank: singles, the highest cards of pairs,
    threes, straights and flushes, and the sets in full houses and four of
    a kinds.

  Jokers
    The pack has two jokers (typed jk). A joker is wild: it stands for
    whichever card makes your combination best. A joker on its own is the
    best single card there is. A joker can't stand in for the three of clubs
    on the first play. Each player is dealt 13 cards as usual, so the last
    two cards aren't used. (Still to settle: who starts if the three of
    clubs is one of those two?)

  Reversal
    Playing a four of a kind reverses the order of every card: 3c becomes
    the best card and 2s the worst. Ranks and suits both turn round, but
    the kinds of five-card hands keep their order. The next player has to
    beat the four of a kind in the new order. Another four of a kind turns
    the order back.)

name pickering_pusoy_dos
extends pusoy_dos

deck standard with jokers

.(replaces the standard game's table of the same name)
values suit_order {
    Clubs 1, Hearts 2, Diamonds 3, Spades 4
}

flag reversed


.(Jokers: try every card each joker could be, and keep the best. Every
  comparison in the standard game goes through strength, so this is the
  only change jokers need.)
def strength(cards){
    return(max version v in cards: base(v))
}


.(Reversal: card_strength gives 5 for the worst card and 56 for the best,
  so 61 minus it turns the order round)
def card_strength(card){
    if(reversed){
        return(61 - base(card))
    }
    return(base(card))
}

.(after a play, not a pass: a four of a kind scores 400 and something)
def after_move(){
    if(passes is 0 & count(middle) is 5 & strength(middle) / 100 is 4){
        reversed = not reversed
    }
    base()
}
